{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLAUDE.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-06T16:22:21.222115Z","id":"9a5a54fe90fff39e479720b59b666e31dc91a1abb63921549ce9dd8f33c0afcd","body":{"detail":"CLAUDE.md:227 reads \"batch 1 to `POST .../graphs/{id}/paths` ..., the rest to `POST .../graphs/{id}/paths/{path_id}/steps`, both `application/x-ndjson`\". The same paragraph later says build.rs maps the body to `text/plain`, and that is what goes on the wire: the generated `open_graph_path`/`append_graph_path_steps` set `CONTENT_TYPE: text/plain` (crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:62-82 rewrite_ndjson_request_bodies; the unit test at crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:1857-1860 asserts `content-type: text/plain`). Someone reading the first sentence to debug a proxy or a server content-type check gets the wrong header. The CHANGELOG entry (CHANGELOG.md:39-41) states it correctly.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"35439beeed6893bf7769e7fbc8969839081e882ba8413f0c23c7ace6fb7befd6"},"suggested_fix":"Say \"both declared `application/x-ndjson` in the spec and sent as `text/plain` by the generated client\" in the first sentence, or drop the content type from it and leave the build.rs sentence.","summary":"CLAUDE.md says both batch routes are `application/x-ndjson`, but the client sends `Content-Type: text/plain`","tags":["review","review:pr-305-r2","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLAUDE.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-06T16:31:16.014081Z","id":"e45fe050e2f3b962422b211b042387331422461d25a089cefee0552699215db7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9a5a54fe90fff39e479720b59b666e31dc91a1abb63921549ce9dd8f33c0afcd","summary":"Confirmed. CLAUDE.md:227 says \"batch 1 to POST .../graphs/{id}/paths ..., the rest to POST .../graphs/{id}/paths/{path_id}/steps, both \\`application/x-ndjson\\`\" and, later in the same bullet, that build.rs maps that body to text/plain. On the wire it is text/plain: the generated open_graph_path sets CONTENT_TYPE to HeaderValue::from_static(\"text/plain\") (target/debug/build/pathbase-client-6437817308489f24/out/pathbase_client.rs:3689-3690), rewrite_ndjson_request_bodies renames the media type at generation time (crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:62-82), and graphs_post_streamed_sends_graph_then_batches asserts \"content-type: text/plain\" on every batch request (cmd_pathbase.rs:1857-1860). CHANGELOG.md:39-41 states it correctly. Kind suggestion is right: a documentation inconsistency.","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLAUDE.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-06T17:07:14.883070Z","id":"180e0c10aec0ea58f2263f682d07ef403db8df08d25acc2f3ca9940e41331350","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5ab5d1d","summary":"Fixed: CLAUDE.md no longer states a content type in the batch-routes sentence; the build.rs sentence (text/plain on the wire) stands.","supersedes":"9a5a54fe90fff39e479720b59b666e31dc91a1abb63921549ce9dd8f33c0afcd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
